{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And the one who burns it — he shall wash his garments.</b> According to the plain sense, all who are occupied with it before the burning do not require washing of garments, for its character is not yet distinguished from other slaughter-offerings, since they too all require slaughter and sprinkling. And Scripture placed the purification of the one who casts before the purification of the one who burns, because the one who casts finishes his service before the one who burns finishes his service."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:38.172953295Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}